Considered dropping `--` entirely, since per-argument classification
makes it redundant: a leading dash is always a flag and everything
else is a branch, so nothing needs a positional separator to be
disambiguated. Kept it as a tolerated (currently inert) separator only
because the flag/branch ordering around `--` may be reworked -- most
likely flipped to the conventional "own args -- pass-through" form --
and accepting the token now is friendlier than rejecting it and having
to start honouring it later.
